endogeneity: Durbin–Wu–Hausman F(1, 2,397) = 7.56   p = 0.006
note: `one` is collinear with the regressors and instruments before it and was dropped from the instruments (line 2)

## nothing left to instrument
let staff = dataset(staff).add(both = age + distance)
staff.ivreg(productivity ~ age + distance + both, instruments: both ~ offer).first_stage()

---
first stage · productivity ~ age + distance + both
nothing is instrumented: the fit dropped every instrumented regressor
note: `both` is collinear with the columns before it and was dropped (line 2)
note: `both` was dropped, so nothing is instrumented and the estimates are those of least squares (line 2)

## a fit by reg has no first stage
let staff = dataset(staff)
staff.reg(productivity ~ training).first_stage()

---
error[Z0401]: `first_stage` cannot be called on a RegFit
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | staff.reg(productivity ~ training).first_stage()
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is a RegFit
  |
  = help: `first_stage` takes an IvFit first; `x.first_stage(...)` is `first_stage(x, ...)`

## kept under a name and exported
let staff = dataset(staff)
let stages = staff.ivreg(productivity ~ training, instruments: training ~ offer + distance).first_stage()
type_of(stages)
stages.export("output/first.tex")

